# Automation: no mock / demo data

Hard rule for **every** Admin Automation tab/page (Dispatch Rules, Champ Scoring, Stacking, Radius Expansion, Vendor Status, Scheduled Tiers, Pay on Delivery, Champ Status, Audit Log, and any future Automation screen):

1. **Never ship or rely on mock/demo data** for Automation UI or its services.
2. Data must come from **live APIs** (and SLA / dispatch rule / policy sources of truth where applicable).
3. Do not add new `*.mock.js` usage for Automation screens; when touching a tab that still has mocks, **replace with real API wiring** — do not extend the mock.
4. Feature flag `automation` (`isAutomationRealApi`) must be the live path; do not leave mock-only pages as the default for production work.
5. Display values (thresholds, toggles, timelines) must not hardcode demo numbers when the backend/SLA already owns them.

When implementing or reviewing any Automation page from now on, apply this rule first.
